# isochron_ML.ode -- isochrons of the Morris-Lecar oscillator, in XPPAUT alone (no BVP)
#
# ======================================================================================
# THE METHOD
# ======================================================================================
# Γ          = the stable limit cycle;  T = its period;  x* = the equilibrium inside Γ
# phase 0    = gamma0, the point of Γ with the largest v
# clock      = theta = t/T (mod 1) for a state on Γ that starts at gamma0
# clock reading (asymptotic phase) of any state x0:
#     integrate x0 until it has settled on Γ
#     s     = time of an upward crossing of v = thr (after settling)
#     tc0   = time of the first upward crossing of thr from gamma0
#     theta(x0) = (tc0 - s)/T  mod 1
#     (x0 then keeps step with the point of Γ at phase theta(x0))
# isochron of phase th = all states with clock reading th
#
# This file integrates three things side by side:
#   A. the "γ copy"   (vg, wg): a state on Γ; it waits at gamma0, then starts so that
#                     its phase is ths + t/T              -> the clock, and a shadow
#   B. the "test copy" (v, w): starts at (px, py), gets a kick dk in v at time thk*T,
#                     aux theta = its clock reading       -> clock reading, PRC, phase slices
#   C. the "backward copy" (vb, wb): runs BACKWARD in time from a point very close to
#                     gamma0 on the straight isochron there, and stops after (k - th) T
#                                                         -> a point of the isochron th
#     why C works: near Γ the isochron of phase 0 through gamma0 is a short straight line
#     (direction (ev, ew), perpendicular to the adjoint Z at gamma0). The flow carries
#     isochron a in time t onto isochron a + t/T. Backward by (k - th) T it carries the
#     isochron 0 onto the isochron -(k - th) = th (mod 1), and backward the points spread
#     out from Γ, so the tiny line becomes the whole isochron.
#
# THE ONE TRICK used below: Initialconds > Range over a parameter, with
#     Reset storage = N, a transient (Numerics > Transient) that skips everything except
#     the settled end of each run, and the curve drawn as points (lt <= 0)
#   -> each run leaves ONE dot; the dots of all runs make the picture.
#
# ======================================================================================
# EXPERIMENTS (in the XPP window)
# ======================================================================================
# 0. Γ, T, gamma0, thr, tc0 (already filled in below; to find them yourself):
#      Initialconds > Go; Initialconds > Last (repeat) -> on Γ
#      Initialconds > Periodic (uses v)                 -> T
#      Data viewer: the row with the largest vg         -> gamma0
#      thr = (min v + max v)/2 on Γ; tc0 = first time vg crosses thr upward from gamma0
#
# 1. THE CLOCK.  Viewaxes > 2D: vg, wg.  Initialconds > Go.
#      Γ is drawn; plot aux clock against t: it runs 0 -> 1 once per period.
#
# 2. THE CLOCK READING of x0 = (px, py) = (-40, 0.35).  Initialconds > Go.
#      Plot aux theta against t: after the transient it is constant = 0.3037.
#      Graphic stuff > Add curve: v against w (test copy) next to vg, wg (Γ).
#    the SHADOW: set ths = 0.3037 (the reading); Initialconds > Go;
#      plot v and vg against t: after the transient the two spike together.
#      (any other ths: they spike at different times, forever)
#    x0 = x*: px = -23.0918, py = 0.158053: it never spikes, no clock reading.
#
# 3. A PHASE SLICE (clock reading along a line):  py = 0.158 (through x*)
#      @ trans=680 (8 T), total=690; Graphic stuff > Edit curve: line type 0 (dots)
#      Initialconds > Range: over px, from -60 to 30, 400 steps, Reset storage N
#      Viewaxes > 2D: x = px0 (aux), y = theta, 0..1:
#      all phases 0..1 are squeezed into a tiny interval of px around x*  (pile-up)
#
# 4. ISOCHRONS by backward integration (the C copy):
#      Viewaxes > 2D: vb, wb; x -70..50, y 0..0.65;  Graphic stuff > Edit curve: lt 0
#      @ trans = k T (= 171 for k = 2), total = trans + 2
#      Initialconds > Range: over u, from -1 to 1, 400 steps, Reset storage N
#      -> the dots lie on the isochron th (default 0.25)
#      change th (0.05, 0.15, ...) and Range again (Reset storage N) -> more isochrons
#      Graphic stuff > Add curve vg, wg (with trans = 0 run first, or Freeze Γ) for Γ.
#    near Γ: zoom in close to Γ -> the isochron is a straight line
#    far from Γ: the isochrons bend, fold around x* and pile up along the line from x* up
#      to the right (the dots crowd into x*)
#    keep k = 1 or 2: Γ attracts so strongly (about 10^4 per period) that backward k = 3
#      throws almost every dot into x* or out of the picture; dec = 12 decades of start
#      distances s are needed to fill the isochron with dots
#
# 5. THE PRC with real kicks.  px = gamma0 v, py = gamma0 w (= 33.3258, 0.305411)
#      dk = 0.2 (a small kick in v); @ trans=680, total=690; lt 0
#      Initialconds > Range: over thk, from 0.005 to 0.995, 100 steps, Reset storage N
#      Viewaxes > 2D: x = kphase (aux), y = dth (aux)  -> PRC: phase shift dth vs kick phase
#      small dk: dth/dk = the infinitesimal PRC  (Numerics > Averaging > New adj, on Γ alone)
#    LARGE KICKS: dk = 8, 17, 29 (10, 20, 35 % of the width of Γ): Range again each time
#      -> far from the infinitesimal PRC; jumps where the kick crosses the pile-up near x*
# ======================================================================================

# --- the model (one copy = fv, fw; every copy below uses the same functions)
minf(x)=.5*(1+tanh((x-va1)/va2))
winf(x)=.5*(1+tanh((x-va3)/va4))
tauw(x)=1/cosh((x-va3)/(2*va4))
fv(x,y)=(i-gl*(x-vl)-gca*minf(x)*(x-vca)-gk*y*(x-vk))/c
fw(x,y)=phi*(winf(x)-y)/tauw(x)
par i=100,c=20,gl=2,vl=-60,gca=4.4,vca=120,gk=8,vk=-84
par va1=-1.2,va2=18,va3=2,va4=30,phi=0.04

# --- numbers of Γ (experiment 0)
par per=85.29064, gv0=33.32581, gw0=0.3054107, thr=-8.505133, tc0=77.87963
# direction of the straight isochron at gamma0 (perpendicular to Z(gamma0)), and x*
par ev=79.91397, ew=-0.1163597
# x* = (-23.09182, 0.1580528)

# --- A. the γ copy: waits at gamma0 until tw, then runs; phase = ths + t/T
par ths=0
!tw=mod(1-ths,1)*per
vg'=fv(vg,wg)*heav(t-tw)
wg'=fw(vg,wg)*heav(t-tw)
init vg=33.32581,wg=0.3054107
aux clock=mod(ths+t/per,1)

# --- B. the test copy: v = px + dv, w = py + dw; kick dk in v at time thk*T
par px=-40,py=0.35,dk=0,thk=0.3
!tk=thk*per
dv'=fv(px+dv,py+dw)
dw'=fw(px+dv,py+dw)
tl'=0
init dv=0,dw=0,tl=0
global 1 t-tk {dv=dv+dk}
global 1 px+dv-thr {tl=t}
aux v=px+dv
aux w=py+dw
thx=mod((tc0-tl)/per,1)
aux theta=thx
aux dth=mod(thx+.5,1)-.5
aux px0=px
aux kphase=thk

# --- C. the backward copy: starts at gamma0 + s (ev, ew), runs backward for (k - th) T
#        s = sign(u) smax 10^(-dec (1 - |u|)): u in [-1, 1] covers both sides, dec decades
par th=0.25,k=2,u=0.5,smax=0.02,dec=12
!tau=(k-th)*per
!s=sign(u)*smax*10^(-dec*(1-abs(u)))
#        it also stops when it leaves the box |v| < 200, |w| < 2 (backward, the states
#        outside Γ run off to infinity)
vbx=gv0+s*ev+dvb
wbx=gw0+s*ew+dwb
go=heav(tau-t)*heav(200-abs(vbx))*heav(2-abs(wbx))
dvb'=-fv(vbx,wbx)*go
dwb'=-fw(vbx,wbx)*go
init dvb=0,dwb=0
aux vb=vbx
aux wb=wbx

@ total=690,dt=0.05,meth=rk4,bound=1e9,maxstor=100000
@ xp=vg,yp=wg,xlo=-70,xhi=50,ylo=0,yhi=0.65
done
